course: dictionary
lesson: 3520
title: Favorite and favourite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Favorite is a word you use when you talk about what you like best. You can have a favorite food, a favorite song or a favorite book. «My favorite animal is the otter.» The word tells you which one you like most out of all the choices.
explain: Favorite can also be a noun. It can mean a person or team that most people think will win. «The Blue Lions are the favorites to win the cup.» Here favorites means the ones most likely to win. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or is it the thing itself?
explain: Favorite can also mean someone who is liked more than others, and that is not always fair. A teacher with one favorite pupil may give that pupil all the best jobs, and the others may feel left out. So the word can describe a choice that feels good to one person and unfair to another.
explain: Spelling depends on where you live. «American spelling dropped the u from words like "color" and "favorite", helped by Noah Webster's dictionary of 1828.» Britain kept «favourite», so both spellings are correct in their own country. Use the spelling your teacher uses.
fact: Favorite means the one you like best.
fact: A favorite can also be a person or team that most people think will win.
fact: In British English the word is spelled favourite, with a u.
fact: «American spelling dropped the u from words like "color" and "favorite".»
fact: In a survey, each favorite is a label for a group you count, such as favorite fruits on a bar graph.
exercise: «Maya's favorite book is about a dragon.» What does favorite mean here? | A book about the sea | The longest book in the library | The one she dislikes most | *The one she likes best
exercise: «The Blue Lions are the favorites to win the cup.» What does favorites mean here? | Teams that never play | Teams that lost last week | The players who wear blue shirts | *The teams most people think will win
exercise: Which spelling of favourite is used in American English? | favoryte | favourite | favrite | *favorite
test: «Lena says her favorite season is autumn, because the leaves turn red.» What does favorite mean? | Her oldest season | Her only season | *The one she likes best | The one she hates most
test: A teacher has a favorite pupil and gives them all the best jobs. What might be unfair about this? | *Other pupils may feel left out | The teacher forgets the date | The class gets bigger | The pupil becomes taller
exam: Which sentence uses favorites as a noun, meaning the ones expected to win? | I like my favorite song best. | Favorite is spelled with a u in America. | *The favorites were the first to cross the finish line. | My favorite lunch is pasta.
